  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sanjay Agrawal vs State Of Odisha .... Opposite Party(S) on 17 May, 2024 In The High Court Of Orissa At Cuttack Crlmc No.818 Of 2024 Sanjay Agrawal .... Petitioner(s) Mr. S. K. Joshi, Advocate -versus- State of Odisha .... Opposite Party(s) Mr. B. K. Ragada, Aga Coram: Justice Sibo Sankar Mishra Order 17.05.2024 Order No. 01. 1. Heard.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2. The Petitioner has challenged the order dated 16.01.2022 passed by the learned J.M.F.C., Kantabanji in G.R. Case No.28 of 2021, whereby the learned Court below has taken cognizance of offences under Sections 420/270/269 of I.P.C. read with Sections 51/53/54/59/61/63 of the Food Safety and Standards Act against him. 3. However, he submits that during investigation, the Petitioner was served a notice under Section 41-A of Cr.P.C. and after the cognizance was taken, summons has been issued against him, therefore, he may be protected. 4."
  },
